  "HDDS-7191": {
    "jira_id": "HDDS-7191",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Implemented",
    "title": "Create separate property for s3 admin ",
    "description": "Currently, all s3 operation via Ozone CLI use `ozone.administrators` or `ozone.administrators.groups` property for define admins who can generate and revoke s3 keys for any user. This approach doesn't provide possibility to split s3 key generation to separate admin groups. \r\n\r\nAs s3 keys are security sensitive it will be useful to have possibility to split responsibility between general admins and special s3 admins. \r\n\r\nSo, my proposal next: \r\n1. Create new props `ozone.s3.administrators` and `ozone.s3.administrators.groups`\r\n2. In case when at least one of these props is defined all s3 shell operation can be executed only by one of defined user as admin. Each user still should have permission to generate keys for itself.\r\n3. In case when these properties are empty admins should be taken from `ozone.administrators` or `ozone.administrators.groups`. \r\n\r\nAs you can see these changes have backward compatibility by point 3.",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "149dfa6a265806f47094c928e822eedf443c11a1",
        "message": "HDDS-7191: Separate prop for s3 admin",
        "author": "Mikhail Pochatkin",
        "date": "2022-08-30T12:52:02Z",
